id: E2183-draft-2301
trigger_tool: conan|make|buildsystem|test_package
phase: source|build|package|consumer-test
error_signature: "installed build metadata not found|NSSHARED.*unset|Makefile.tools.*No such file|consumer.*cannot.*archive"
severity: 2
category: packaging|build-system|consumer-validation
match_keywords: no-arch build scripts, makefile fragments, NSSHARED, Conan buildenv_info, consumer archive
root_cause: A build-system-only upstream release can have no compiled artifact, so a package that merely reports a successful no-op build does not prove that its installed makefile fragments are usable. Consumers also fail when the package path is not exported consistently.
affected_scope: No-arch Conan packages that install makefile fragments, helper scripts, or other build metadata consumed by downstream native builds.
verification_cmd: "run the upstream test target; assert installed fragment and helper paths; export NSSHARED; compile and archive a small consumer through the packaged fragments"
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: install-layout-plus-real-consumer
rec_description: Preserve the upstream share layout, expose its root through Conan build/run environment metadata, and add a consumer fixture that invokes the installed build fragments with a real compiler and archiver.
rec_command: "make test; set NSSHARED=<package>/share/netsurf-buildsystem; make -C <consumer> all"
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: recipe-and-test
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: fragment-smoke
fallback_description: If a target compiler is unavailable, validate every installed fragment and helper identity and run make's parser in dry-run mode; do not claim native consumer success.
fallback_command: "test -f <fragment>; make -n -C <consumer> all"
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: validation
forbid_1_pattern: "mark.*build.*pass.*without.*consumer"
forbid_1_reason: A no-op upstream target does not exercise the package's installed interface.
forbid_1_consequence: Broken NSSHARED paths or missing makefile fragments can reach downstream users undetected.
forbid_2_pattern: "copy.*buildsystem.*to.*flat.*package.*root"
forbid_2_reason: Consumers rely on the upstream share/netsurf-buildsystem directory layout.
forbid_2_consequence: Existing NetSurf makefiles resolve the wrong NSBUILD/NSSHARED path.
principles: P007, P018
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
